  "answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions with a focus on security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in Q3 2023 (July 15th) with a call for ideas from R&D by July 20th to leverage AI in data visualization. Significant progress was made in Phase Two, achieving a breakthrough in predictive analytics, with a detailed report scheduled for November 20th. The project secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate, an AI research leader. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the successful testing of a prototype for secure file sharing ahead of schedule. The launch date is set for September 12, 2024. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, will be updated effective January next year. A celebration for the testing milestone is planned for October 10th."
